'''Nivell de Seguretat''' is a private security company headquartered in [[Sant Bart]], [[Jala Province|Jala]], [[Balboa]]. Founded in 1992, the company is publicly traded on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] under the ticker symbol NDS. It provides a range of private security services, including manned guarding for businesses and industrial facilities, cash-in-transit transport for banks and financial institutions, remote monitoring and surveillance, and alarm response. Nivell de Seguretat is one of the principal private security firms operating in Balboa and serves clients across the country from its headquarters in Sant Bart and regional offices in [[Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Portblanc]].

== History ==

Nivell de Seguretat was founded in 1992 in [[Sant Bart]] during the period of economic liberalisation and privatisation that followed the end of the Cold War. The company was established to meet the growing demand for private security services from the commercial and industrial sectors, particularly in the [[Badia Curta]] industrial zone and the canal corridor, where the expansion of manufacturing, logistics, and financial services had outpaced the capacity of the National Police Force to provide dedicated security for private premises.

The company initially focused on manned guarding for industrial facilities in the Jala highlands, serving the chemical and aluminium plants of the Badia Curta complex. In the mid-1990s, Nivell de Seguretat expanded into cash-in-transit services, securing contracts with several regional banks for the transport of currency, bullion, and other valuables between branches, ATMs, and central clearing facilities. The expansion into cash transport was driven by the growth of the financial sector in [[Sant Cristòfor]] and the increasing volume of cash transactions in the canal corridor.

In the 2000s, the company invested in remote monitoring technology, establishing a central monitoring station at its Sant Bart headquarters and offering remote surveillance and alarm response services to commercial clients. The monitoring division became a significant component of the company's operations, serving retail chains, office buildings, and industrial sites across Balboa.

Nivell de Seguretat completed an initial public offering on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] and has been publicly traded under the ticker symbol NDS since the late 1990s. The listing provided capital for the company's expansion into remote monitoring and its nationwide cash-in-transit network.

== Services ==

Nivell de Seguretat's operations are organised into three principal service divisions.

The manned guarding division provides uniformed security officers for businesses, industrial facilities, government buildings, and commercial properties. The division's largest contracts are with chemical and manufacturing companies in the [[Badia Curta]] industrial zone, where Nivell de Seguretat personnel control access, monitor perimeters, and provide round-the-clock security for plant facilities and storage depots.

The cash-in-transit division provides secure transport of currency, bullion, and other valuables for banks, retailers, and financial institutions. The division operates a fleet of armoured vehicles from depots in [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Sant Bart]], and [[Portblanc]], servicing ATMs, bank branches, and retail clients across the country. Nivell de Seguretat is one of the principal cash-in-transit operators in Balboa, competing with a small number of domestic and international firms.

The remote monitoring division operates a central monitoring station at the company's Sant Bart headquarters, providing 24-hour surveillance and alarm response for commercial and industrial clients. The division uses CCTV, access control, and intrusion detection systems to monitor client premises and dispatch response teams in the event of an alarm activation.

== Operations ==

Nivell de Seguretat is headquartered in [[Sant Bart]] and maintains regional offices in [[Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Portblanc]]. The company's client base is concentrated in the canal corridor and the Jala industrial belt, with a growing presence in the Tramuntana highlands and the eastern provinces. The company employs trained security personnel licensed under Balboan private security regulations and operates in compliance with the regulatory framework governing the private security industry.

The company's Sant Bart headquarters houses its central monitoring station, administrative offices, and a training facility for security personnel. The Sant Cristòfor regional office coordinates cash-in-transit operations and corporate security contracts in the canal corridor, while the Portblanc office serves the western provinces and the canal zone's logistics corridor.

== Controversies ==

=== 2021 Carretera Gran Presa del Nord protest and Hernandez Lee lawsuit ===

{{main|2021 Carretera Gran Presa del Nord protest|Hernandez Lee}}

On 8 March 2021, Nivell de Seguretat guards were deployed to provide security at the construction site of the Nou Gran Presa Carretera in the [[La Serra de Llevant]] comarca of [[Tramuntana Province]], where the [[Moviment del poble Birú]] (MPB) had organised a sit-in protest against the road's planned route through Birú sacred caves. During the protest, NdS guard [[Jonaes Mendosas i Vidal]] was involved in a physical altercation with [[Hernandez Lee]], a 23-year-old protester and MPB member. After the protest concluded, Mendosas followed Lee in a NdS vehicle, kidnapped him, and killed him. Lee's body was discovered on 24 March 2021. Mendosas was arrested on 10 March and was subsequently convicted of kidnapping and murder in 2022 and sentenced to life imprisonment.

The family of Hernandez Lee filed a civil lawsuit against Nivell de Seguretat in 2021, alleging that the company was liable for Mendosas's actions under the doctrine of {{w|vicarious liability}}. The family argued that NdS had failed to properly screen, train, and supervise its security personnel and that the company's deployment of guards to the protest site had created the conditions for the confrontation and subsequent kidnapping. Nivell de Seguretat contested the lawsuit, arguing that Mendosas had acted outside the scope of his employment and without the knowledge or authorisation of the company.

In 2023, the court found Nivell de Seguretat not liable for the death of Hernandez Lee, ruling that Mendosas's actions were outside the scope of his employment and that the company had not been negligent in its hiring or training practices. The ruling was controversial and was criticised by the [[Moviment del poble Birú]] and the [[Socialist Front of Balboa]] (FSB), who argued that the company should bear responsibility for the actions of its employees. The case was cited during the [[2026 Balboa data center protests]] as an example of the perceived impunity of private security firms operating at protest sites.

